    narr:narration """This narrative argues that [the vendor stays the system of record for reference data until the last site is live](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36), grounded in [the drift risk of split ownership — divergence discovered via a mis-priced consignment weeks later](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_38). [An accountability corollary](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_39) keeps blame with the vendor through the programme, and [site-team assent](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_41) folds it into [a steering-group summary of the rollout cadence](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_42). The arc opens on [the framing question of when ownership actually transfers](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_34). A second session adds a hidden dependency: [the rule assumes one cutover window open at a time, and would need rewriting under a parallel rollout](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25), which draws [a decision to stay sequential](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_26). Nothing here records the vendor's own agreement.""" ;
